 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nParser fails with UnboundLocalError when parsing Databricks dollar-quoted strings\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen parsing Databricks SQL with dollar-quoted strings, the parser raises an `UnboundLocalError` for the variable `tags`. This happens when trying to parse valid Databricks syntax like function definitions with Python code blocks.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport sqlglot\n\n# This should work but raises UnboundLocalError\nsql = \"\"\"CREATE FUNCTION add_one(x INT) RETURNS INT LANGUAGE PYTHON AS $$def add_one(x):\n  return x+1$$\"\"\"\n\ntry:\n    result = sqlglot.transpile(sql, read='databricks')\n    print(\"Success:\", result)\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(\"Error:\", e)\n```\n\nThe error occurs when the parser encounters the `$$` delimiter and tries to process the dollar-quoted string but fails due to an undefined `tags` variable.\n\n#### Expected Behavior\n\nThe parser should successfully parse dollar-quoted strings in Databricks SQL without raising UnboundLocalError.\n</issue>\n",
